---
description: PIXINIT session rules. Read the short context files, not the repo.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read only `.cursor/context.md`, `.cursor/disks.md`, and `.cursor/tasks.md` before editing.
Do not read the rest of the repo. Open a source file only when `tasks.md` names it.
Edit only the files listed in `tasks.md`.
Do not invent SMART values. Live reads must use the formulas in `disks.md`.
NO HARDCODE: No serial/model/firmware/temp/host values in .cs/.xaml. All live from SMART/Identify. disks.md is for testing only.
If SMART or Identify is missing, show Unavailable plus the reason and the fix. Do not fill a stand-in health, temperature, or host total.
After the edit, run the Release build and the harness. Reply with the diff and the test result only.
